    "embedding_text": "控制板有持续咔哒声 Control Board Clicking Continuously\n1 先断开所有的配件及机臂，重新上电看看\n2 如果还是响那么排查一下电源，按遥控器后是不是有电源压降大导致继电器无法保持吸合，如果电源没问题， 就是控制板坏；\n3 如果没有异响了，再排查下是否是机臂或者配件的影响，把机臂或配件一个一个接回去，接一个测试一个，再看看有什么异常",
    "content_zh": "1 先断开所有的配件及机臂，重新上电看看\n2 如果还是响那么排查一下电源，按遥控器后是不是有电源压降大导致继电器无法保持吸合，如果电源没问题， 就是控制板坏；\n3 如果没有异响了，再排查下是否是机臂或者配件的影响，把机臂或配件一个一个接回去，接一个测试一个，再看看有什么异常",
    "content_en": "1 Disconnect all wired accessories and the gate arm from the control board, leaving only power connections. Then, turn the power of the system off and on.\n2 If the noise continues, check the voltage at the +BAT- terminals (11#, 12#) while pressing the remote.\nIf the reading remains stable at approximately 24V (above 22V), the control board is likely defective.\nIf the voltage is unstable or low, disconnect the power cable from the control board and test the output voltage of the TCS3 controller directly to see if it is above 22VDC and stable.\n3 If the noise stops after Step 1, the motor or a wired accessory is the cause. To identify it, first reconnect only the motor and test. If the noise does not return, proceed to reconnect accessories one at a time, testing after each connection, until the faulty part is found.",
