    "content_en": "May I ask if the arm cannot make any sound when the remote is pressed.\n1 Check the control board\nSwap the wire connections of the two gate opener arms on the control board. If the same arm remains faulty, the issue is with the arm itself. If the issue moves to the other arm, the problem is likely with the control board.\n2 Check the faulty arm motor\nConnect the RED and BLACK wires of the faulty arm directly to the 24VDC batteries to check if the arm operates normally. Switching the polarity (by swapping RED and BLACK wires) will reverse the arm's direction. If the arm does not run, the motor inside the arm is faulty. If the arm runs in both directions, proceed to Step 3.\n3 Check the limit switch\nReconnect the RED and BLACK wires of the faulty arm back to the control board. Disconnect the BLUE, GREEN, and YELLOW wires of the faulty arm from the control board. Use two jumper wires to short the ULT, COM & DLT terminals to which the wires were connected, and then press the remote to see if the arm can extend and retract. During this test, press the remote in time to stop the arm in case it extends too far. Then use the remote to reverse the direction. If the arm can move in both directions, the limit switch is faulty.",
