    "content_en": "Ensure that the wires of the limit switch (BLUE, GREEN, and YELLOW wires of the arm) are not shorted. Confirm that each wire is properly inserted into its corresponding terminal and is not twisted with any other wire.\nPlease readjust the Open Position. The open position is adjusted by Limit Switch B (located far from the motor). Adjust Limit Switch B inward on the arm, then press the remote to open the gate and see if the open position changes. Repeat the operation several times to check if the arm consistently stops at the new position.\nIf it changes, adjust Limit Switch B to the desired open position and tighten the screw.\nIf the problem persists, rotate the Front Mount 180° and test again.\nIf there is still no luck, the limit switch might be defective.\nEnsure that the wires of the limit switch (BLUE, GREEN, and YELLOW wires of the arm) are not shorted. Confirm that each wire is properly inserted into its corresponding terminal and is not twisted with any other wire.\nPlease readjust the Close Position. The close position is adjusted by Limit Switch B (located far from the motor). Adjust Limit Switch B inward on the arm, then press the remote to close the gate and see if the close position changes. Repeat the operation several times to check if the arm consistently stops at the new position.\nIf it changes, adjust Limit Switch B to the desired close position and tighten the screw.\nIf the problem persists, rotate the Front Mount 180° and test again.\nIf there is still no luck, the limit switch might be defective.",
