    "question": "手动反推来排查+电阻",
    "embedding_text": null,
    "content_zh": "如果不想并接的话，也可以反推排查试试，虽然不是很精准。\n1 给门施加持续的相反的力，看看门是否可以开或者关到位\n2 如果第一步起作用，那要检查门的铰链，托架螺栓是否紧固，连接处是否有明显磨损或者螺栓断裂的情况；\n3 如果第二步没发现问题，那就需要加电阻，如果门只一个方向走停，还需要加二极管；电阻没极性，二极管有极性，二极管控制着哪个方向施加阻力，所以二极管的极性要接对（the direction of the diode polarity controls whether the resistor load is applied during open or closing and that if the diode is removed then the load is applied in both cases）\n注意链接国家\n如果门只一个方向走停，还需要加电阻+二极管；电阻没极性，二极管有极性，二极管控制着哪个方向施加阻力，所以二极管的极性要接对\n加电阻和二极管\n拉开门开门不正常加二极管电阻 （推开门关门不正常）\n注意链接国家\n拉开门关门不正常加二极管电阻（推开门开门不正常）\n注意链接国家\n加了电阻之后，相当于增大了负载，需要加大遇阻力。\n测电机电流\n万用表测机臂电流\n除了HJ4022的其他平开门机，机臂运行时候的电机电流应该大于0.5A 小于3A, 如果机器运行时候的电机电流大于3A，那说明负载过载或者电机有问题（可以机臂从门上拿下来排查）\n测机臂空载电机电流 小于1A 是正常的 大于1A 说明电机有问题\n测工作电流详细步骤\n测机臂空载电流",
    "content_en": "1 Push against (in the opposite direction of the gate moving) the gate during the gate is opening/closing, continuously add some load to the gate and see if the gate can open/close all the way properly. If it works, then the working current through the arm is so small that the opener could only extend and retract few inches. Please proceed to next steps.\n2 If step 1 worked, please double check the gate's hinges and brackets for tightness, and inspect all connection points for significant wear or broken bolts.\n3 If the problem persists, adding some load to the gate motor by connecting a resistor to the BLACK & RED wires of the arm in parallel to solve the problem. Regretfully, we do not have this resistor for sale in our store. Sorry for the inconvenience.\nBelow is the link to the resistor that will work.\n4 After adding the resistor, you need to increase the FORCE. Please power off the system first (disconnect the power source from the +BAT- terminals). And turn the FORCE potentiometer all the way clockwise to increase the stall force. Then turn on the power and operate the gate opener to run for a complete opening & closing cycle. See whether the gate will open and close all the way in the next opening and closing cycle.\nConnect anode of the diode to “+Motor” (connect with the red wire of the motor in parallel), connect cathode of the diode to one side of the resistor, then connect the other side of the resistor to “Motor-” (connect with the black wire of the motor in parallel). Please refer to the diagram below. Here are the links for the resistor and diode from third parties that are compatible.\nResistor:\nDiode:\nConnect anode of the diode to “Motor-” terminal (connect with the black wire of the motor in parallel), connect cathode of the diode to one side of the resistor, then connect the other side of the resistor to +motor (connect with the red wire of the motor in parallel). Please refer to the diagram below. Here are the links for the resistor and diode from third parties that are compatible.\nResistor:\nDiode:\nAfter adding the resistor, you need to increase the FORCE. Please power off the system first (disconnect the power source from the +BAT- terminals). And turn the FORCE potentiometer all the way clockwise to increase the stall force. Then turn on the power and operate the gate opener to run for a complete opening & closing cycle. See whether the gate will open and close all the way in the next opening and closing cycle.\nMeasuring DC Current going through the arm with a Multimeter like this. Switch ON the multimeter. Turn the knob to test DC current. Please connect the Multimeter pens in series with the power supply and the arm. The arm can only operate normally with the current lower than 3Ampere.\n1. Power off the opener system first.\n2. Disconnect the red wire of the arm from the +motor terminal on the control board.\n3. Connect the positive polarity (e.g. red pen) of the multimeter to the +motor terminal on the control board.\n4. Connect the red wire of the arm with the negative polarity of the multimeter (e.g. black pen) together.\n5. Turn the knob of the multimeter to test DC current.\n6. Power on the opener system and press the remote to detect the value on the multimeter. The normal value should be lower than 3 Amps.\nMeasuring DC Current going through the arm with a Multimeter like this. Switch ON the multimeter. Turn the knob to test DC current. Please connect the Multimeter in series with the power supply and the arm. The arm can only operate normally with the current lower than 1 Ampere.",
